{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Implemented and pushed as Gerrit change 2560 (https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/2560).\n\nWritten RED first: the new test file failed on missing _WARN_CROSS_SESSION and on the literal still being present in _execute.py, then went green after the implementation.\n\nAC1: derive_policy_sets now emits _WARN_CROSS_SESSION and _execute.py consumes it; its frozenset literal is gone (asserted).\nAC2: membership pinned against the exact 14 the literal carried — the refactor provably moves no policy.\nAC3: every warn name is a live route name, asserted as a subset of live ROUTES.\nAC4: renaming a flagged route carries the warning; a retired flagged route contributes nothing.\nAC5: _WARN_CROSS_SESSION is named in _CENSUS_SETS and added to the overlay skip list in _all_current_spellings, so test_derive_covers_exactly_the_census_set_names passes and the spelling census does not double-count.\n\nOne design decision the plan left open, and it matters. Six of the 14 routes are built by comprehensions over a name tuple, so there was no per-route constructor to edit. The tempting move was a local warn = {...} set plus warn_cross_session=name in warn, which is exactly the existing legacy_output idiom three lines away in the same function. I did NOT do that: it would have reproduced the very bug this ticket fixes, because renaming a spelling in names would leave the warn entry stale and silently drop the warning again. Instead the name tuples now carry (spelling, warns) pairs, so the flag rides the definition site and a rename is atomic.\n\nI deliberately left the adjacent legacy_output set alone. It has the same staleness shape, but churning it is outside this reviewed plan — and going beyond the plan is what got ce8f and e755 refused at close earlier today.\n\nModule size: _registry.py is 708 lines. At its former 800 this change could not have landed at all, which is precisely why bc66 was made a prerequisite rather than folded in.\n\nGates: make lint and make typecheck clean; 596 passed / 3 skipped in tests/unit -k \"registry or execute or cross_session or policy\". Mutations: unflagging a route, flagging an unflagged one, and dropping the census key each turn the suite red."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788413908480535001,"uuid":"ef1488cb-5a16-43b6-8ab6-271bce2adb06"}